# Default Role Guidance

This section helps determine primary vs supporting vs contextual behavior.

## Primary patterns should usually come from:

- entry_quality
- exit_quality
- scaling_quality
- strong position_structure patterns

These families usually contain richer composite patterns.

---

## Supporting patterns should usually come from:

- entry_context
- trade_excursion
- broad position building facts

These are often useful evidence but not the best top-line summary.

---

## Contextual patterns should usually come from:

- execution frequency
- trade duration
- trade closure
- broader overlapping entry-range facts

These add structure but usually should not dominate the story.

